ILLIT is a powerhouse five-member South Korean girl group formed by Belift Lab, a prominent sub-label under HYBE Corporation. The group's lineup—comprising Yunah, Minju, Moka, Wonhee, and Iroha—was meticulously selected through the intensive 2023 JTBC survival audition program R U Next? They officially burst onto the global music scene on March 25, 2024, with the release of their highly anticipated debut extended play, Super Real Me. Fueled by the whimsical, high-energy lead single Magnetic, the group achieved immediate commercial success and unprecedented viral fame across social media platforms. The track's addictive pluggnb and house beats, paired with memorable point choreography, resonated deeply with international audiences. This explosive reception allowed ILLIT to shatter multiple industry milestones, notably becoming the fastest K-pop group in history to enter the US Billboard Hot 100 with a debut track, while also marking the first time a K-pop debut song entered the UK Official Singles Chart. Backed by their dedicated global fandom, known officially as GLLIT, the members have rapidly established themselves as leading figures of K-pop's fifth generation, widely recognized for their youthful concepts, distinct vocals, and seamless synchronized performances.

